title: 'The "untouched" filter already exists: his fork''s subscribee folder lists just the messages he has neither hidden nor filed, and counts them.'
pid: 401118c5-0a4d-4b86-afd2-b651e5bdb0fd
body: |2-
  In his fork, Top's 'to Jeff' stands under "It subscribes to these."
  with the herald 'C32/35': 32 of 35 messages not yet integrated.
  Drawn editable, it shows exactly those 32, in Top's order, with the
  3 he hid in a folded folder of their own. His server drew that for
  him, folded, at 17:19 UTC.
  So the motion Top offered him,
  [[id:5eacc0a8-0088-4c11-82cb-88e315331bad][a way to stop only on mail nobody has touched]], would give Jeff
  nothing he lacks. Top can read the same list with no code: view
  '7642d4d5-e66c-4aac-b985-a1d75132e674' and make the subscribee
  editable ('editable' in its handle with skg-for-ai, 'C-c s e' in
  Emacs). On a server where Jeff's fork is foreign the subscribee is
  drawn write-protected, its messages undrawn, until that request.
